"""Download new videos from selected feeds as Opus audio.

Reads a feed list. YouTube channel feeds are read as RSS, and the uploads
playlist is checked only when that request fails. Other RSS and Atom feeds
are read directly, and a channel or playlist URL is read with yt-dlp.
Livestreams and archived livestreams (stream VODs) are not saved. Regular
uploads are extracted with yt-dlp and ffmpeg to Opus.

Runs on Linux. It needs python3, yt-dlp, and an ffmpeg build with libopus.
This program is free software under the GNU GPL, version 3 or later.
See the LICENSE file.
"""

